-- section 4.11 pointer-check elision: polymorphic-dispatch soundness trap
-- @req: OPT-03, OPT-07, OQ-08
-- @expected-pass-after: phase-37
-- XFAIL (phase-37): a checked pointer as a FUNCTION PARAMETER (`ptr: *Friendly`
-- below) is not implemented in codegen. Two gaps, one of which needs a design
-- decision:
--   1. emit_val_is_any_fat_ptr / emit_fat_ptr_pointee_type_c key off the
--      producing instruction (HEAP_ALLOC / ARENA_ALLOC / ADDR_OF). Parameters
--      have no producing instr, so `ptr.level` emits `_v2.level` on an
--      Iron_FatPtr and fails to compile. Reproduces without any interface:
--      `func get(p: *P) -> Int { return p.x }`.
--   2. The gen check cannot be lowered. gencheck_deref_needs_check picks one of
--      three NON-interchangeable helpers (iron_check_pointer_gen /
--      _stack_pointer_gen / _arena_pointer_gen) from the STATIC IronLIR_GenSource
--      on the producing ADDR_OF. A parameter's gen source is caller-dependent, so
--      there is nothing to read it from -- and mistagging is exactly the
--      "checked by the heap helper and read garbage" pitfall lir.h:195-202 warns
--      about. Carrying the tag at runtime would have to widen Iron_FatPtr, which
--      is ABI-frozen at 16B by static_assert (iron_runtime.h:159-172).
-- Emitting the deref without the check would compile and print the right answer
-- while silently dropping the very check this fixture exists to pin, so it is
-- left failing rather than papered over.
-- extends-spec: POINTER-CHECK-ELISION.md soundness trap "polymorphic dispatch
-- joins" — a generation check straddles a virtual/interface method call
-- resolved at runtime. A naive elision that trusted a single implementation's
-- (clean) may-free summary would be unsound: the call site's effective summary
-- must be the JOIN over every implementation, which is conservatively may-free
-- until a per-call-site type-set narrows it (deferred). The indirect call is
-- therefore a may-free barrier and the check is PRESERVED. This run uses an
-- implementation that does not free, so the value prints correctly.

interface Greeter {
    func greet() -> Int
}

object Friendly impl Greeter {
    val level: Int

    func greet() -> Int {
        return self.level
    }
}

func run(g: Greeter, ptr: *Friendly) {
    -- virtual dispatch through the interface — opaque may-free join
    val n = g.greet()
    println("greeted: {n}")
    -- deref AFTER the indirect call — its gen-check must NOT be elided
    println("after dispatch: {ptr.level}")
}

func main() {
    val f = Friendly(9)
    println("before: {f.level}")
    run(f, &f)
}
